Changelog: 19-11-2026 21:14:53

Fixed. install-requirements.sh installs the RPM packages and the development extras with dnf on a flattened image (no /run/ostree-booted, such as a PS5 image, where rpm-ostree is masked and failed with "not booted via libostree"); an Atomic image still layers them with rpm-ostree. The HINT lines of the tests name the same command (install_cmd), and the NVMe power-saving hint points to cmdline.txt instead of rpm-ostree kargs.

